<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- SCRUM-91 point of no return, RETAINED AS AN APPLIED NO-OP. The written mandate
         PROJECTION is retired by the shared-core bootstrap now: MRG's 000 carries the
         identical guarded drop all ten M-services carry, which is what makes the drop safe
         from any service in any order (nothing serializes the ten migrations, so no copy of
         it may depend on another service having gone first).

         THIS CHANGESET STAYS because it EXECUTED on the standing cluster and applied
         changesets are immutable. Its tableExists guard MARK_RANs wherever 000 has already
         taken the table, which is every reachable database state, so it costs one guard
         evaluation; deleting the file would orphan a history row to no end.

         WHY IT ORIGINALLY LIVED HERE, and why it no longer needs to: MRG's own
         003-man-ext-status-view built man_ext_status with "FROM mandate", and CockroachDB
         refuses an un-cascaded drop while a view selects from the table, so a drop ordered at
         000 killed the migration. SCRUM-91 removed that changeset, so MRG builds no view over
         the projection at all and the drop belongs where the siblings keep it. Any standing
         copy of the view is retired by 006, which the master includes ahead of 000.

         mandate_reason_code is NOT touched: it is reference data, not projection state. -->

    <changeSet id="009-drop-mandate-projection" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><tableExists tableName="mandate"/></preConditions>
        <dropTable tableName="mandate"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
